WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:09.820
Remember the context of Putin's announcement.

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:17.590
He wants to ease the Western sanctions on
Russia, and he wants to do it by portraying

00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:24.820
Russia, portraying himself as not just the
king-maker in the Middle East, but also a

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:25.820
peacemaker.

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:31.020
This announcement was made in advance of the
so-called peace talks in Geneva, and Putin

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:36.250
wanted to impress the West, primarily the
White House by his efforts to withdraw the

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:42.980
troops or lower, let's not say withdraw, lower
the number of troops and jets and so on, in

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:45.030
order to promote peace.

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:53.600
Given the economic situation in Russia, foreign
policy is something that greatly strengthens

00:00:53.600 --> 00:01:00.030
devotion to Putin, which in turn is the cornerstone
of regime's legitimacy.

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:04.970
Putin needs a lot of victories in foreign
policy, and he can get far more victories

00:01:04.970 --> 00:01:07.400
still in Syria.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:11.299
So what do you think of Putin’s permanent
strategy?

00:01:11.299 --> 00:01:14.979
Please let us know in the comment section,
and please let us know if there’s anything

00:01:14.979 --> 00:01:17.459
else you want us to cover in 60 seconds.

